# Changelog

Write changelog for **what users perceive**, not how we implemented it.

**Audience:** `@oceanbase/design` / `@oceanbase/ui` / related package consumers, and design-system users (designers + frontend devs).

## Include

- New or changed component API, behavior, or visuals
- Bug fixes users would notice
- Public developer tools they adopt (CLI, MCP, Figma Code Connect in Figma)
- Breaking changes and migration notes (call out explicitly)

## Exclude

- File paths, folder layout, colocation strategy
- CI, build config, lint, internal scripts, Agent Skill plumbing
- Counts or inventories unless they define the user benefit
- Details that do not affect runtime, public API, docs, or design workflow

Pure internal work → PR changelog: `No user-facing changes` / `无用户可感知变更`. Skip post-commit changelog unless asked.

## Formats

| When | Format |
|------|--------|
| PR body | Bilingual table per `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`; cell content is **raw markdown** aligned with `docs/design/design-CHANGELOG.md` (see `.cursor/skills/github-pr-submit/SKILL.md`) |
| After commit (chat) | Same **style** as `docs/design/design-CHANGELOG.md` — output in chat only; **do not edit** changelog files |
| `docs/design/design-CHANGELOG.md` / `.zh-CN.md` | **Release only** — batch update when cutting a release; never on feature PRs or after commit unless user explicitly asks for a release changelog pass |
| Package `*CHANGELOG.md` (`design` / `ui` / `charts` / `codemod`) | Release maintainer only; do not edit on every PR unless requested |

## Do not auto-edit changelog files

Agents and contributors **must not** modify `docs/design/design-CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/design/design-CHANGELOG.zh-CN.md`, or package `*CHANGELOG.md` as part of normal feature work, commit follow-up, or “done” cleanup.

- **During development / PR:** changelog lives in the **PR body table** only.
- **After commit:** if the user asks for 更新日志, reply in **chat** using the design-CHANGELOG **format** — do not write into repo files.
- **At release:** release maintainer consolidates entries into the official changelog files in one pass.

Full guide and examples: `.cursor/skills/github-pr-submit/SKILL.md`（Changelog 章节）
